Hello again,

My Caveman finally ascended. After the Quest the game was really easy,
but I wanted this character to be really prepared for the end game. This
was, after all, the first char I started after a long pause away from
playing Nethack. So, no conducts here, I just used every trick I knew in
order to survive. I genocided, I wished, I polymorphed, I danced with
nurses, with wraiths, you get the idea. 

Funny that the first game should be an ascencion, I'd like that trend to
continue :D 

The game started pretty uneventful, no grand luck or especially scary
moments either. Level 3 had a big scroll shop so I price-ID'ed the scroll
of identify   early in the game. The shop also had a scroll of genocide,
but I didn't use it until a bit later. Minetown had a cross-aligned altar,
and a magic lamp in the light shop. I blessed the lamp and #rubbed it, but
the ungrateful djinn didn't give me a wish, instead remained peaceful. I
C)alled him Ungrateful Bastard. Sokoban had the amulet and it helped me
survive until the Castle. 

When I found the Medusa level I still had no magic resistnace, was not
high level enough for the Quest and didn't have any means of levitation.
So I used a ring of polymorph control and a wand and turned myself into a
master mind flayer in order to be able to get to the Castle. Before I went
I genocided all ; so an oilskin cloak was not needed. Funny, I had
completely forgot that I needed an amulet of unchanging. I had quite a
jump when I turned back into human form somewhere inside the Castle. I
managed to get out into the main dungeon by freezing a path on Medusa's
level with a wand of cold. 

There was a gray dragon in the Castle so I made myself GDSM and used the
wand of wishing for magic markers, later for speed boots and gauntlets of
power. About that time I genocided L (the bastards). The last wish went
for a ring of free action, but that was only after I had marked the
Vibrating square. 

The Quest was easy, maybe even too easy. With a scroll of scare monster on
the upstairs, the Chromatic Dragon didn't offer any resistance. After I
got the Sceptre of Might I didn't use any other weapon for the rest of the
game. 

Before going into Gehennom I searched hard for Ludios, and it was very
good that I did so. Ludios is a great source of food (for staying in the
dungeon as long as you want) and gold (for donating to priests). Gehennom
itself was boring as hell, had to map it manually. A fun moment: Orcus
summoned Yeenoghu while I was wielding a rubber chicken :D. None of them
had a chance do cause any trouble, plus this way I got the wand of death
completely unused. This was very useful, as it was the only wand of death
I ever saw in the game. A not so fun moment: a master mind flayer ate my
brain a bit and I forgot a ***-load of items and levels. I had to go back
up and re-map all the lost levels up to the first. 

Somewhere before the Wizard I had accumulated 3 scrolls of genocide, and
decided the best way to use them would be to dance a bit with some nurses.
Only after the second scroll I remembered that nurses disappear faster
when you're at full health. Duh. The third scroll I used wisely, however,
and got my health to ~350. 

With HP of 350 and AC of -48 the end game was not difficult at all. Rodney
only showed up 4 times. I switched conflict on just after I killed him for
the first time, and never switched it off until the altar on the Astral
plane. The method for discovering the portals was confused scroll of gold
detection, only on Water I had to search for it the hard way - with all ;
genocided I could afford it. I only had to use a full healing potion once
in the end game, and that was on Air. 

I didn't mean to use conflict on the Astral plane, I just forgot to switch
it off before stepping on the portal. Ishtar immediately sent some hostile
angels, but then I decided to keep conflict on. The right altar was the
right one (heh), guarded by Famine.I turned conflict off, quaffed all the
healing potions, and offered the Amulet. 

The voice of Ishtar rings out: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--





